  "text" : "Here's the shape of it.\nOne diagram Risk appetite in pounds flows down through principles, controls, enforcement versioned, so a bump is proportionality moving as the world moves.\nEvidence flows back up, minus what each permissive choice still leaves exposed, into one number.\nThe balance sheet, flux, distributes it.\nKaiveno enforces it.\nEvery beat I'm about to show you is one piece of this hourglass.\nStart with how it ships.\nPolicy is just a dependency, a lint packupin, sign and a doc by pull request.\nRight now, two sign policy versions coexisting\neach judging only the workloads that claim it, with no shared webhook and no last right wins race between them.\nOne version array controls the lot.\nTry to run a version outside that array and the orphan guard refuses it every time proven, not promised.\nAnd the compliant path is the easy path.\nFlip a workload from version one to version two, and suddenly it needs a read-only five system.\nOur CI catches it offline before MergeWatch version one passes.\nVersion 2 fails exactly where it should.\nThat failure never reaches a cluster.\nIt never reaches production.\nNo pager goes off at midnight for something CI already caught at lunchtime."
